{
  "dom_id": "step-t1422",
  "name": "Introduction",
  "problem": "Suppose we want to represent the following number line graph using interval notation:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14191664/assets/0bf5e420e2929032c11964e15d710014fb34d559aa065428b9d57fff14d10eb0.png)\n\nThis number line consists of the interval $(-3, -1)$ as well as the interval $(1, 3).$\n\nTo express the combination of these two intervals, we create a **union of intervals** using the **union sign** $\\cup$ as follows: \n\n$$\n(-3, -1) \\cup (1, 3)\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
